  "id": "rotational-row",
  "name": "Rotational Row",
  "definition": "A unilateral kettlebell row from a hand-supported hip hinge that deliberately combines shoulder extension from flexion, scapular retraction, elbow flexion, and upper-body spinal rotation while both feet, hips, and knees remain position-held. The exact admitted fixture rows toward the armpit and turns the shoulders and upper back over the working side before a controlled return. Strict non-rotational rows, accidental momentum twists, pelvis- or leg-driven turns, unsupported rows, renegade rows, and cable or dumbbell variants remain outside this narrow family. The catalog represents the deliberate turn as spinal rotation without claiming isolated thoracic motion or side-specific oblique recruitment.",
